# Autonomous Trading System - Cursor Development Rules
# Minimize tokens. Maximize clarity. No redundant explanations.

## 1. CODE STYLE & STRUCTURE
- **Python 3.11+**, type hints mandatory (mypy strict mode)
- Use DuckDB + Polars for data ops, not Pandas
- QuantLib for options pricing (BSM for NSE, Black-76 for MCX)
- OpenAlgo as broker abstraction layer
- Redis for state sync between Oracle VPS and Lambda
- All execution logic: deterministic, testable, no randomness except jitter in backoff
- All AI logic: async, Lambda-bound, never touches hot path

## 2. FILE ORGANIZATION
```
trading_system/
├── infra/
│   ├── vps_core.py          # Oracle VPS persistent layer (WebSocket, order books, state)
